WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0080: a solid effect piece keeps its depth write.

BG3 masks a spell's solid (unblended) pieces with its own depth, inside the effects pass: one recipe
lays the mesh down with an alpha test and a depth write (zw1, greater-or-equal, a fragment shader
with an OpKill), and the next draws the colour with an EQUAL test, no write and no discard of its
own. The replay forced `depth_write_enabled: false` on every draw, so the EQUAL draws failed
everywhere and Grease's blob and splash never arrived; forcing their test to greater-or-equal
instead (tried 2026-10-28) drew the whole unmasked billboard, a black quad and black shards.

Now a draw writes depth exactly when BG3's recipe says it does. The replay's depth is its own copy
of WoW's (`wowbg3_fx_depth`, written by the prep pass), so WoW's own depth is untouched; it is reset
before the over-white run as well, so the over-black and over-white pair still answers the same
question at every pixel and T = W - C stays right.

That attachment can no longer be sampled while it is written, so the prep pass also writes the same
depth into a colour target (`wowbg3_fx_depth_copy`, R32Float) and a draw that reads BG3's scene
depth (special key 1) reads that. It holds the depth as the effects pass began, which is what BG3's
own copy holds.

